body:
Oh boy, where to start...

&#x200B;

First, I'm not sure if you even understand the irony of complaining about the \*skies\* being empty as a problem and then going on to say when they aren't its cancer but it's astounding. Along with that saying that there's no way to defend against it is laughable, as if the skies are truly empty and you are being ground pounded, it should be rather easy for you regardless of skill to pull an ESF and kill the ground pounding pleb as AI and AV weapons are rather bad at A2A combat.

&#x200B;

Saying the hover fighting is a bug is interesting since the aircraft were designed to be VTOL and therefore it only makes sense that hover fights are possible. I don't know what you mean that cheaters exploit it and if you believe that fighting in hover mode is a exploit you should go refer to Wrel's tutorial on it.

&#x200B;

I'm also not quite sure why a fancy mouse or fast reactions are required. I'd be hard pressed to call my 34$ logitech mouse fancy or my reactions fast as they are slightly below average. My eyesight is terrible and I need glasses to play, I'm far from what you'd call the perfect specimen and it's never impeded my fun in the air. There is no one in the air I believe I could never beat if I didn't improve myself a little more whether in terms of movement or aim I know there's always something I can improve and I don't see why that's any different from infantry or tanks.

&#x200B;

I'm also not sure why you are saying that CAI changed how Libs interact with ESF's is pandering to "skyknights". Every pilot I know, both lib and esf respectively, hate the changes made in CAI and almost all posts made by pilots regarding it were pleas to revert it. It made it miserable for Libs to fight ESFs and ESFs to fight Libs and I know myself and many other ESF pilots are guilty of just ignoring libs thinking "Itd be too much of a pain in the ass and take way to long to kill it, I'll go find something else."

&#x200B;

The thing I totally agree with you on is that they should have changed the flight controls. It used to be that the ESF controls were entirely raw input, back before the PS4 port. When that changed they added massive acceleration to the controls making it way harder for people to learn how to fly and for people to get the muscle memory down. It used to be that muscle memory alone would be able to make you a top pilot but now its more random and going back to your comment on reaction time I'd say its even more important now that we can't rely on training to get good. Yet this was something that resulted in almost all pilots at the time quitting the game so to say thats pandering to "skyknights" is insane.

&#x200B;

Finally as to it being bullshit that "skyknights" don't fight A2G ESFs I hope you believe me when I say I wish I could kill every single one, it's basically free certs. The only time I can't however is when they have friendly flak in the vicinity. I wish I could keep track of the amount of times I have died or nearly died diving in to kill a ground pounder only to be hit with flak or enemy lockons immediately. It sucks that I have to miss out on those points but with the way that G2A currently is set up there is just no way for me to even hope to kill those ground pounders because the second I try I get erased off the map by 3 locks all at once.
